& [Purpose]
  + make the published no-argument one-shot semantic inspection host consumable through exact portable coordinates fixtures and caller-owned transcript acceptance without creating a generic launcher or application adapter

& [SJSProcessing]
  + delineation selects contract identity raw byte transcript outcome deterministic replay receipt and development-only fixture proof
  + refinement separates process transport success semantic success verified transcript executable identity and installed application acceptance
  + constraint reapplication retains the unmodified wire and stdio host and all their source and non-authority bounds
  + pruning removes executable-path configuration generic launch policies service lifecycles storage MCP provider model remote identity and application mutations from the consumer library
  + seven-fold exhaustion finds a pure transcript verifier plus golden handoff bundle smaller than a new process runtime
  + data design admits exact request stdout stderr exit values and exports only sealed read-only receipt coordinates

& [Requirements]
  + [CICH-001] preserve the published source lineage current Pinky authority shared C checkout and foreign narrative
  + [CICH-002] add one safe-Rust effect-free library cantor_sop_inspect_consumer and workspace membership without modifying the published wire or stdio implementation
  + [CICH-003] define one strict versioned portable contract with zero arguments observed EOF single exact JSON response fixed host fault exit0 or exit2 and inherited wire bounds
  + [CICH-004] bind the contract to kernel.sop.semantic-inspect request response profiles non-authority and a domain-separated canonical digest
  + [CICH-005] parse contract bytes through strict unknown duplicate trailing profile and raw-size refusal and compare every coordinate to the supported contract
  + [CICH-006] admit only caller-owned request stdout stderr and integer exit values; library performs no I/O process launch clock environment or path resolution
  + [CICH-007] bound raw request at MAX_WIRE_REQUEST_BYTES plus one stdout at MAX_WIRE_RESPONSE_BYTES and stderr at128 bytes before dispatch
  + [CICH-008] classify valid zero-argument outer input with exit0 empty stderr and byte-identical deterministic wire response as inspection_succeeded or semantic_refused
  + [CICH-009] classify invalid empty oversized or malformed outer input only with exit2 empty stdout and exact cantor_stdio_host_refused newline stderr as host_refused
  + [CICH-010] refuse unexplained nonzero exit missing output partial output alternate payload extra stderr signals unsupported exit values and valid-input public host faults without a receipt
  + [CICH-011] reject semantically equivalent but nonidentical stdout including suffix whitespace reordered JSON changed nested data and recomputed foreign response seals
  + [CICH-012] seal a receipt over contract digest raw request stdout stderr SHA256 byte counts exit outcome optional wire coordinates and explicit non-authority
  + [CICH-013] validate receipts by exact reconstruction from the supplied transcript rather than trusting receipt hashes or producer declarations
  + [CICH-014] parse bounded strict receipt bytes without implying full transcript acceptance from shape parsing alone
  + [CICH-015] retain eight deterministic exact fixtures for Unicode success empty result two-page pagination nested refusal malformed unknown-field and empty outer input
  + [CICH-016] bind each fixture request and expected stdout stderr exit and receipt; regenerating the fixture bundle must be byte-identical
  + [CICH-017] fresh-process development tests replay all eight fixtures through the published stdio executable in debug and overflow-checked release
  + [CICH-018] bound development harness output capture and whole exchange timeout drain both outputs concurrently close stdin and kill the child on abandoned exchange
  + [CICH-019] test consumer contract receipt byte transcript mutation and bounds adversaries plus static no-effect dependency/source absence
  + [CICH-020] document EOF versus MCP JSONL framing semantic versus host refusal and independent application ownership with no messaging or installed-consumer claims
  + [CICH-021] retain component artifact identities actual focused/workspace gate summaries adversarial evidence and requirement-by-requirement proof
  + [CICH-022] pass locked offline serialized focused debug release warnings-denied Clippy format bounded replay and recursive evidence gates before completion publication
  + [CICH-023] run proportionate complete current-tree workspace debug release and Clippy gates after implementation has settled with fresh Python shim if required
  + [CICH-024] record exact per-element graph source justification narrative staged inventory completion signature non-force publication direct remote equality and immediate bookend

& [AcceptanceGates]
  + [CICH-A01] exact golden bundle regenerates and all eight fresh-process transcripts validate against the unmodified wire
  + [CICH-A02] every unsupported contract transcript or receipt adversary refuses without authority or a false success receipt
  + [CICH-A03] library is effect-free and development subprocess capture is bounded and distinct from product launch authority
  + [CICH-A04] exact retained artifact hashes and actual test results support all twenty-four requirements
  + [CICH-A05] consumer documentation and handoff cite pinned lineage and leave application launch installation and acceptance outside
  + [CICH-A06] signed completion is published only after exact attributable gates and immediate non-force bookend

& [NonAuthority]
  + a verified transcript proves deterministic correspondence of supplied bytes not actual process execution trusted executable identity model quality operator approval or application acceptance
  + no production subprocess filesystem listener resident service storage cache database MCP LSP provider model shell installation update remote machine message merge or publication authority

& [State]
  + formed_for_exact_effect_free_consumer_implementation_and_development_fixture_proof
